'''Nhuwala''' is an extinct<ref>{{Cite web |title=Glottolog 5.1 - Nhuwala |url=https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/nhuw1239 |access-date=2025-02-10 |website=glottolog.org}}</ref> [[Pama–Nyungan languages|Pama–Nyungan language]] of [[Western Australia]]. Dench (1995) believed there was insufficient data to enable it to be confidently classified, but Bowern & Koch (2004) include it among the [[Ngayarda languages]] without proviso.<ref>Bowern & Koch (2004) ''Australian Languages: Classification and the Comparative Method''</ref>

== Names ==
Alternate names for Nhuwala include Nuala, Ngoala, Noella, Noanamaronga, Nooanamaronga, Jawanmala, Nunkaberi and Noala.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Did you know Nhuwala is severely endangered? |url=https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/4853 |access-date=2025-02-10 |website=Endangered Languages |language=en |archive-date=18 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250118034223/https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/4853 |url-status=dead }}</ref>

